source. Everything not allowed below is reserved to XCraftTM.

1. Using the Software

   You may download the official releases of the Software and use them, for
   free, for any purpose, including making bots you sell or run for others.

2. Your projects and your bots

   Projects you make with the Software are yours. Bots you export with it
   contain the XC Circuit runtime; you may run them and give them to others
   as exported, as long as this notice stays in them. You may not take the
   runtime out of an exported bot to use it on its own or in other software.

3. Your plugins

   You may write plugins for the Software (blocks, build modes, pin types,
   themes, translations) through its plugin interfaces, and share or sell
   them under terms of your choice. Your plugins are yours; this licence
   doesn't cover them, and they may not include parts of the Software beyond
   what its plugin interfaces need.

4. Contributing to the Software

   You may view the source code, and fork, clone, build and change it, only
   to try out and propose changes to the Software, such as new blocks,
   translations or fixes, through pull requests to its official repository
   (github.com/XCraftTM/XC-Circuit).

   You may not publish, distribute, sell or host the Software, changed or
   not, or builds of it, or substantial parts of it, nor use its code in
   other software. A fork on GitHub that only serves proposing changes is
   fine.

5. Your contributions

   By proposing a contribution (a pull request, patch, translation, block or
   other change), you confirm you have the right to give it, and you grant
   XCraftTM a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, free and irrevocable
   licence to use, change, sublicense and distribute it under any terms,
   this licence included. You keep the copyright of your contribution.

6. Names and logo

   "XC", "XC™ Circuit" and the logo are not licensed to you. Don't use them
   for your own software or plugins in a way that suggests they are official.

7. Other people's work

   The Software includes work by others under their own licences: Rust
